Description: Fix the file-header size check added for CVE-2015-2063
 The bounds check from 006_security-afl.patch adds 4 bytes for ADDSIZE and then
 28 for the file header, but those 28 bytes begin with PSIZE, which *is* the
 ADDSIZE field. Every file header (they always carry ADDSIZE) therefore failed the
 check and was silently skipped, so unace 1.2b-24..27 extracts and lists nothing.
 Count the shared field once; the check itself stays.
Author: The412Banner
Forwarded: no

--- a/unace.c
+++ b/unace.c
@@ -186,7 +186,9 @@
          memcpy(mhead.AV, tp, mhead.AV_SIZE);
          break;
       case FILE_BLK:
-         need_size += 28;
+         /* The 28 bytes below start with PSIZE, which is the ADDSIZE field
+            already counted above when ACE_ADDSIZE is set. */
+         need_size += (head.HEAD_FLAGS & ACE_ADDSIZE) ? 24 : 28;
          if (need_size > head.HEAD_SIZE)
             return 0;
          fhead.PSIZE     =BUFP2LONG(tp);
